<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:trl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Trials;assembly=OpenRigs.Trials"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>Zapit's trials on ZapitDaq (ZapitTrials is MATLAB Zapit's), the same in every task: give it the trials' rules (TrialRules, once, at Go). In an optogenetics experiment (the rules' Laser, a LaserTiming, is set) each trial is armed at its Arm event, during the interval (ArmZapit: a ZapitDaq Arm with its condition, laser on at the trial's power or off), into Zapit.Commands; ZapitDaq builds the buffer from the session's bank and the trigger line starts it. The laser's stop is the rules' Laser: LaserTiming.ForDuration plays it for its laserDurationSeconds; LaserTiming.UntilOutcome and UntilStimulusOff (no duration, UntilStopped) play it until an early stop (ZapitEarlyStop: the ramp, then laser and LED at 0 V), sent once per trial from its trigger at whichever comes first of its outcome (UntilOutcome) or LaserOff (UntilStimulusOff: its StimulusOff, else its outcome), its LaserCap (the rules' LaserCapSeconds on the Harp clock) or LaserBackstop (LaserCapSeconds on the computer's clock, should the board stall: the one wall-clock wait). The ZapitTrigger line is raised at each Trigger and cleared at each TriggerOff (SetZapitTriggerLine, on BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands). TrialLoop checks ZapitDaq's Armed events (Zapit.Events). Needs TrialEvents, Zapit.Commands (OpenRigs.Devices ConnectForTaskZapitDaq) and ZapitTriggerLine from the workflow.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
        <Name>Source1</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>Optogenetics?</Name>
        <Description>An optogenetics experiment: the rules have a laser.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Laser != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Laser</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
        <Name>Zapit</Name>
        <Description>Once at Go, with the rules' laser timing (ZapitLaser): each trial's Arm, and its early stop when the laser has no duration.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>ZapitLaser</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Arm</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>ArmZapit</Name>
              <Description>Each trial's Arm (its condition, laser on at the trial's power or off, for the trial's own laser duration (an ILaserDurationTrial) unless the rules' laser plays until stopped (UntilStopped), else until its early stop), sent during the interval: ZapitDaq builds the buffer and waits on the trigger line.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:ZapitDaqTrialCommand" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Trigger</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ZapitLaser</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>UntilStopped?</Name>
              <Description>A laser until the outcome or the stimulus off (LaserTiming.UntilOutcome, UntilStimulusOff) plays until stopped early.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item2.End != "AfterDuration"</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>LaserOnUntilStopped</Name>
              <Description>From the trigger, stops the trial early once: at its outcome (UntilOutcome) or its LaserOff (UntilStimulusOff), at its LaserCap (the rules' LaserCapSeconds on the Harp clock), or at LaserCapSeconds on the wall clock (LaserBackstop), should the board stall. ZapitDaq plays the ramp, then laser and LED at 0 V; its buffer ends at maxTrialSeconds whatever happens. A trial that ends before its trigger has no laser; the next Arm replaces it.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Name>LaserBackstop</Name>
                    <Description>The trial again the rules' LaserCapSeconds after the trigger on the computer's clock, should the Harp board stall so that LaserCap never comes: the one wall-clock wait. Whichever comes first stops the laser.</Description>
                    <Combinator xsi:type="trl:ZapitLaserBackstop" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                      <trl:Kind>Outcome</trl:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ZapitLaser</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionCondition">
                    <scr:Name>AtOutcome?</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>The outcome stops only a laser until the outcome (UntilOutcome).</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>Item2.End == "AtOutcome"</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1.Trial</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                      <trl:Kind>LaserCap</trl:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Trial</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                      <trl:Kind>LaserOff</trl:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Trial</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="trl:ZapitEarlyStop" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="14" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="14" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source4" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
</Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ZapitLaser</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="UntilStopped" Selector="UntilStopped" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
          <trl:Kind>Trigger</trl:Kind>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Set>true</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
          <trl:Kind>TriggerOff</trl:Kind>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Set>false</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Name>TwinTrigger</Name>
        <Description>The same trigger as ZapitDaq's Trigger command: the simulated twin's edge, so a desk run starts each trial at the loop's trigger as a rig's line does. The NI DAQ ignores it.</Description>
        <Combinator xsi:type="trl:ZapitTwinTrigger" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="10" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
